- **Loss of Neuroscience:** Neurons are not isolated cells. They are tightly linked to other cells (e.g., astrocytes, oligodendrocytes, microlagia) that provide neurological and physiological support. Neurodegenerative diseases often disrupt these connections, further impairing neural functioning.

