\[
\text{Oxygen consumption} = \text{CO}_2 \text{ production} \times \frac{\text{CO}_2 \text{ per oxygen consumed}}{\text{CO}_2 \text{ produced}}
\]

The oxygen consumption rate (VCO2) is typically measured in milliliters of oxygen per minute per kilogram of body weight (mL/min/kg).

