The reactivity of the metal in the oxide determines whether it can be reduced by carbon. Metals that are more reactive than carbon can be reduced by carbon.  
- **Al₂O₃ (Aluminum oxide):** Aluminum is more reactive than carbon, so it can be reduced by carbon.  
- **PbO (Lead oxide):** Lead is more reactive than carbon, so it can be reduced by carbon.  
- **ZnO (Zinc oxide):** Zinc and carbon have similar reactivity. Zinc oxide is not easily reduced by carbon. It requires hydrogen gas for reduction.  
- **Fe₂O₃ (Iron oxide):** Iron is more reactive than carbon, so it can be reduced by carbon (in the production of iron from its oxide).  

