\[
\Phi = \frac{GM}{4\pi \varepsilon_0}
\]  
Here, \( \varepsilon_0 \) is the permittivity of free space. The original statement \( 4\pi GM \) is incorrect. The flux through the entire cube is \( \frac{GM}{4\pi \epsilon_0} \). Since the cube has 6 faces, the flux through each face is \( \frac{1}{6} \times \frac{GM}{4\pi \varepsilon_0} = \frac{GM}{24\pi \varepsilon_0} \). Thus, the total flux through all sides is \( 6 \times \frac{GM}{24\pi \varepsilon_0} = \frac{GM}{4\pi \varepsilon_0} \).  

