The probability of getting exactly $k$ heads in $n$ flips is given by the binomial probability formula:
\[
P(X = k) = \binom{n}{k} p^k (1 - p)^{n - k}
\]
where $n$ is the number of flips, $k$ is the number of heads, and $p$ is the probability of getting a head in a single flip. In this case, $n = 12$ and $p = 0.5$.

1. Probability of exactly 9 heads:
\[
P(X = 9) = \binom{12}{9} (0.5)^9 (0.5)^{12 - 9} = \binom{12}{9} (0.5)^9 (0.5)^3 = \binom{12}{9} (0.5)^{12} = \frac{12!}{9!3!} (0.5)^{12} = \frac{12 \times 11 \times 10}{3 \times 2 \times 1} (0.5)^{12} = 220 \times (0.5)^{12} = \frac{220}{4096}
\]

