","Let the side length of the cube be 2 units. Let the radius of each sphere be $r$. The center of the cube is at the point $(1, 1, 1)$. The center of the central sphere is at the center of the cube, so its center is at $(1, 1, 1)$.

The center of one of the other spheres is tangent to two faces of the cube and to the center sphere. Let this sphere be tangent to the faces $x = 0$ and $y = 0$. The center of this sphere is at $(r, r, z)$, where $z$ is the $z$-coordinate. Since the sphere is tangent to the center sphere, the distance between their centers is $2r$. The center of the center sphere is at $(1, 1, 1)$, so the distance between $(r, r, z)$ and $(1, 1, 1)$ is $2r$. Using the distance formula:
\[ \sqrt{(1 - r)^2 + (1 - r)^2 + (1 - z)^2} = 2r \]
Squaring both sides:
\[ (1 - r)^2 + (1 - r)^2 + (1 - z)^2 = 4r^2 \]
