The conservation of momentum equation is:
\[
m_b v_b + m_e v_e = 0
\]
Solving for \(v_e\):
\[
v_e = -\frac{m_b v_b}{m_e}
\]
Substituting the given values:
\[
v_e = -\frac{(1 \text{ kg})(90.0 \text{ m/s})}{5.97 \times 10^{24} \text{ kg}} = -\frac{90.0}{5.97 \times 10^{24}} \text{ m/s}
\]
Calculating the value:
\[
v_e \approx -1.51 \times 10^{-23} \text{ m/s}
\]
The negative sign indicates that the Earth moves in the opposite direction of the ball. The approximate recoil velocity of the Earth is \(1.51 \times 10^{-23} \text{ m/s}\).

