\]

where:
- \( \lambda_{\text{scatter}} \) is the wavelength of the scattered photon,
- \( \lambda_{\text{incident}} \) is the wavelength of the incident photon,
- \( \lambda_0 = \frac{hc}{E} = \frac{hc}{\hbar \omega} \) is the Compton wavelength,
- \( \theta_{\text{max}} \) is the maximum scattering angle, which is \( \theta_{\text{max}} = 180^\circ \) (back scattering).

Substituting \( \theta_{\text{max}} = 180^\circ \) and \( \cos 180^\circ = -1 \):

\[
\Delta \lambda_{\text{max}} = \lambda_0 (1 - (-1)) = 2 \lambda_0.
\]

