\[
\Delta E \Delta t \approx \hbar
\]

where \(\hbar = \frac{h}{2\pi} \approx 1.054 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s}\) is the reduced Planck constant.

First, we need to convert the given decay time from seconds to Joules:

\[
\Delta t = 2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}
\]

Now, we can find the uncertainty in energy:

\[
\Delta E \approx \frac{\hbar}{\Delta t} = \frac{1.054 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s}}{2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}} = 5.27 \times 10^{-12} \text{ J}
\]

